    <solution><me>\mbox{div}\,{\vec{F}} = 6x + 8y + 8z.</me>
So, if <m>W</m> is the interior of the box, we have
<me>\int_{S}\vec{F} \cdot d\vec{A} = \int_{W}(6x + 8y + 8z)dV
= \int_{3}^{4}\int_{0}^{1}\int_{0}^{3}(6x + 8y + 8z)dz\,dy\,dx.</me>
Integrating through each of the integrals in turn, we have
<me>\int_{S}\vec{F} \cdot d\vec{A} =
\int_{3}^{4}\int_{0}^{1} 6x\,z + 8y\,z + 4z^{2}\bigg|_{z=0}^{z=3}\,
dy\,dx</me>
<me>= \int_{3}^{4}\int_{0}^{1} 18 x + 24 y + 36\,dy\,dx</me>
<me>= \int_{3}^{4} 18 x y + 12 y^2 + 36 y\bigg|_{y=0}^{y=1}\,dx</me>
<me>= \int_{3}^{4} 18 x + 12 + 36\, dx</me>
<me>= 9 x^2 + 12 x + 36 x\bigg|_{x=3}^{x=4}</me>
<me>= 111.</me>




Finding flux directly, note that on the faces <m>x=4</m> and <m>x=3</m> the
normal vectors to the surfaces are <m>\vec i</m> and <m>-\vec i</m> respectively,
so that <m>\vec F\cdot d\vec A = \pm 3x^{2}\,dy\,dz</m> (where <m>x</m> is evaluated
at 4 or 3), and similarly on
<m>y = 1</m> and <m>y = 0</m>, and <m>z = 3</m> and <m>z = 0</m>,
<m>\vec F\cdot d\vec A = \pm 4y^{2}\,dx\,dz</m> and
<m>\vec F\cdot d\vec A = \pm 4z^{2}\,dx\,dy</m>, respectively.  Thus on
<m>y = 0</m> and <m>z = 0</m> the flux is zero.  On the remaining faces,
we have



(1) On <m>x = 4</m>,
<m>\vec F\cdot d\vec A =
\int_{0}^{1}\int_{0}^{3}\,48\,dz\,dy =
144</m>;



(2) On <m>x = 3</m>,
<m>\vec F\cdot d\vec A =
\int_{0}^{1}\int_{0}^{3}\,27\,dz\,dy =
-81</m>;



(3) On <m>y = 1</m>,
<m>\vec F\cdot d\vec A =
\int_{3}^{4}\int_{0}^{3}\,4\,dz\,dx =
12</m>; and



(4) On <m>z = 3</m>,
<m>\vec F\cdot d\vec A =
\int_{3}^{4}\int_{0}^{1}\,36\,dy\,dx =
36</m>.
Thus the total flux is the sum of these,
<m>\vec F\cdot d\vec A = 111</m>.



</solution>
